        "math_academy_id": "q-182121",
        "problem": "Find the value of $f(x)=\u2308x{e}^{x}\u2309$ at $x=2.1.$",
        "worked_solution": "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $\u2308x\u2309$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\u2308x\u2309=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n-1<x\\le n,\\,n\\in Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=2.1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2.1) & =\u23082.1{e}^{2.1}\u2309 \\\\  & =\u230817.148\\,95\u2026\u2309.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\u230817.148\\,95\u2026\u2309=18.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2.1) & =\u230817.148\\,95\u2026\u2309 \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
